From 874ec266db06b568c9bd6b5486473c0ae7560712 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:59:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Run queue: submit configs, one warm runner per GPU on pelee
 and rondeau, scorecards at the end

- tools/submit.sh: copies configs into the clone's queue (queue/queue/, shared by both servers through the RAID),
  oldest first; skips a config whose experiment is already queued or running, or whose output folder already has a run
  (--force to rerun it).
- tools/runner.jl: one Julia process per GPU. Claims the oldest job by an atomic rename into queue/running/ (with a
  .claim: host, GPU, process, long, start), only when no other process is on its GPU and, for [queue] long = true, when
  fewer than $PANARCTIC_MAX_LONG (2) long jobs run on its server. Runs panarctic.jl in a fresh anonymous module, then
  the scorecard (unless the config's post_run_analysis wrote it), clears the module and frees the GPU; moves the job to
  done/ or failed/ (.error) and adds a line to queue/summary.md. Exits with 75 before a job whose method overrides
  (partial_cell_fix, catke_under_ice, atmospheric pressure) differ from those loaded, so a fresh Julia takes it; exits
  after 15 min ($PANARCTIC_IDLE_MINUTES) with nothing to run. Jobs left by a dead runner of the same server go to
  failed/. Ctrl-C marks the job interrupted and stops the runner.
- tools/runner_loop.sh: restarts the runner (75: at once; a crash: after 30 s; 0 or Ctrl-C: stops), with
  CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID so GPU numbers match nvidia-smi.
- tools/start_runners.sh [gpus]: one tmux session per GPU (runner-<host>-g<gpu>, default all four), logged to
  ~/logs/. tools/qstat.sh: waiting, running (with status.txt), last finished, runner sessions.
- .gitignore: queue/.
- config_smoke_test_queue_1.toml, _2.toml (100 km, 2 days; one with post_run_analysis, one without);
  config_sep2005_30d_tanh_lim2_nz100.toml, the baseline with 100 levels (top cell 3.8 m instead of 7.8 m): the test
  of the Arctic interior's remaining salinity dipole, as the queue's first real job.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
